ood green smell of Willowmere village. A detective, she reflected, is only a neighbor who pays attention.\n\nMiss Violet Crowe brought flowers — 'for the best detective in the county,' they said, gruff as ever. Mildred Quill put them in water and told them not to be silly, but she kept the card.\n\nAnd if another mystery comes to Willowmere village — as mysteries do, like weather — Mildred Quill will be ready, kettle on, journal open. For truth will out, always, in Willowmere village and everywhere."}]}

